    description: "The execution of the scope amendment. elixir 155 rows (29.4%), haskell 68 (31.5%), swift 38 (36.5%), go 33 (17.4%), python's 4 ungoverned plus django.db.models 29 (the owner ruled django moves too).\n\nRULING 8 IS THE PART THAT PREVENTS A REPEAT: scope gates exist for 6 of 14 languages, and the eight without one (go, elixir, erlang, haskell, swift, objc, c, cpp) are exactly where the rows accumulated. That asymmetry is the mechanical cause, not bad luck.\n\nTHE HIGH_RISK GUARD MUST WIDEN FIRST OR IN THE SAME PR. golang.org/x/sys/execabs.Command / .CommandContext sit in HIGH_RISK_PRIMITIVES and .LookPath in HIGH_RISK_EXEMPTIONS_SUBPROCESS; the WI-gitad phantom-detection direction requires every entry to resolve against a catalogue. Widen the corpus to built-ins PLUS shipped default overlays -- intent preserved exactly (no entry resolving to nothing anywhere), and it removes the one genuine cost WI-bahid identified for the Go cull.\n\nDIRECTION OF RISK: this makes the tool report LESS on a run that does not load the overlays. Measure before shipping, not after. Depends on the default-overlay leg landing first, or the cull strands the rows.\n\nCLOSES: WI-sutuk (project-wide), WI-bahid (the Go case)."  # 343a
    fields: {}  # 343a
- op: discuss  # bb16
  at: '2026-08-28T16:15:09Z'  # bb16
  by: agent  # bb16
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bb16
  clock: 2  # bb16
  nonce: bb16  # bb16
  message: "UNBLOCKED, AND YOUR NUMBERS ARE STALE. Checked 2026-08-28 against dev\ne60cc88f5d.\n\nUNBLOCKED: this item's stated dependency -- \"depends on the default-overlay leg\nlanding first, or the cull strands the rows\" -- was satisfied today by WI-riros\n(PR #598). Shipped community overlays now load by default and disclose\nthemselves, so there is somewhere for the culled rows to land.\n\nTHE FIGURES IN THIS DESCRIPTION NO LONGER MATCH THE TREE. Total rows per\ncatalogue, then vs now:\n\n    elixir    528 -> 529   (+1)\n    haskell   216 -> 179   (-37)\n    swift     104 -> 107   (+3)\n    go        190 -> 193   (+3)\n    python    222 -> 464   (+242)\n\npython's +242 is the 2026-08-15 stdlib climb, which landed four days after the\ncensus was taken; the \"4 ungoverned\" residue (aiohttp.web, flask.Flask, ujson,\nuvicorn) must be re-confirmed against the current file before it is acted on.\n\nHASKELL'S -37 IS MINE, TODAY (INV-nular, #602/#606), and it moves your numerator\nas well as your denominator: I removed the 31 in-process db_* rows plus\nNetwork.Socket socket/bind/listen/close/gracefulClose. `network` is third-party\nby this item's own stricter line, so five of the 68 haskell rows you plan to\ncull are already gone.\n\nAND 26 elixir THIRD-PARTY ROWS CHANGED BOUNDARY WITHOUT CHANGING COUNT (#609).\nPhoenix.Controller / Plug.Conn / Phoenix.Channel / Phoenix.Endpoint response\nhelpers moved net_recv -> net_send. A row census sees nothing; a cull that\ncarries boundary along must not carry the OLD one.\n\nTHE MECHANICAL OBSTACLE, which is the part worth planning around.\n`IoBoundaryCatalog.is_stdlib_module` cannot tell you which rows to move: it\nreturns 100.0% third-party for elixir, haskell, swift AND go, because only\npython declares a `stdlib_modules` list, so the predicate is False for every\nmodule in the other four. That is RECOGNITION, not provenance (the INV-buzab\ndistinction), and here it yields a number that is not imprecise but meaningless\n-- it is also precisely why python is the only language whose numerator survived\nmy re-check.\n\nSo the 155 / 68 / 38 / 33 figures rest on a HAND-CURATED module classification\nthat lives nowhere in the repo -- only as the family lists in WI-sutuk's\ndescription (Ecto, Phoenix, HTTPoison, Req, Tesla, Mint, Postgrex, Redix, MyXQL,\nFinch, Oban; SwiftNIO, swift-log, AsyncHTTPClient, NIOSSL;\nbytestring/text/network). Whichever way you go, the selection has to be written\ndown as part of this PR or the next stdlib climb re-creates the drift silently.\nRuling 8's scope gates are what stop the recurrence, so the curated list and the\ngates want to be the same artifact if possible.\n\nDIRECTION note, restated because it is now measurable: this item says \"makes the\ntool report LESS on a run that does not load the overlays. Measure before\nshipping, not after.\" The INV-nular A/B rig does exactly that and is reusable --\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nular_ab_08282026/ has run.sh, arm.sh, extract.py, a\n7-repo cohort and a per-arm cache; f5_ab_ adds a NETWORK claims file, which\nmatters here because the standing claims file is host_fs-ONLY and would show\nnothing for a network-row cull."  # bb16
- op: discuss  # 5fc1
  at: '2026-08-28T19:47:28Z'  # 5fc1
  by: agent  # 5fc1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5fc1
  clock: 3  # 5fc1
  nonce: 5fc1  # 5fc1
  message: "DONE. Both rulings executed together and MEASURED BEFORE SHIPPING, as this item\nrequired. Branch jgstern-agent/refactor/surun-catalogue-scope, commit 8f36725c37.\n\nTHE CULL: 293 rows out of five catalogues into five shipped community overlays\nthat load by default -- elixir 144, haskell 43, swift 38, go 33, python 33.\nLOSSLESS AND CHECKED, NOT ASSERTED: across all 15 catalogues, catalogue+overlays\nis row-for-row identical to before (same qualified names, same boundaries),\nwith one intended deletion.\n\nTHE ONE DELETION: erlang `http_client.request` is a PHANTOM -- no OTP module by\nthat name, inets' client `httpc` sits one row above it. Deleted rather than\nrelocated because an overlay row would assert a package that does not exist.\nWI-lunav's rule (\"is the crossing still represented\") is satisfied on POSITIVE\nevidence: across ejabberd and emqx, `http_client` matched 0 times, `httpc` 10\nand 9.\n\nTHE GATES: one parametrised gate over every shipped catalogue, allowlist rather\nthan denylist (a denylist is the hardcoded inventory that let execabs and grpc\nin). Its table IS the curated list this item said existed nowhere but WI-sutuk's\nprose, each entry carrying its reasoning. The language list is derived from\nio_primitives/*.yaml, which also closed a live hole: CATALOG_LANGUAGES hardcodes\n14 while the tree ships 15, so bash.yaml sat outside it AND outside the WI-sugav\nsubprocess drift guard it feeds.\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEM.\n\n(1) THE HIGH_RISK PREREQUISITE WAS ALREADY MET. This item says the guard \"must\nwiden first or in the same PR\". It does not: the guard calls load_catalog(lang)\nbare, include_defaults defaults to True, so its corpus already spans shipped\noverlays. Verified the strong way rather than by reading -- after the move, both\nguard directions PASS with all three execabs entries resolving FROM THE OVERLAY.\n#598 delivered it; no widening was written.\n\n(2) ELIXIR IS 144, NOT 155 OR 145. The gate first reported 145 because\n`http_client` is inherited from the erlang parent and counted twice. go 33,\nswift 38 and python 33 matched this item's figures exactly.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/surun_ab_08282026/RESULT.md).\nSequential arms, per-arm cache, canary read OLD and NEW unanimously. Cohort: one\nrepo per culled language, each verified to CONTAIN the culled rows first.\n\n  CONTROL, default io-boundaries: UNCHANGED on all five\n      (517/42/8/1216/1375 edges, identical both arms).\n  DECLARED RISK, --no-default-overlays: reports less, as predicted --\n      pretix -846 edges (-70.4%), plausible -139 (-26.9%), postgrest -5,\n      vault -1, vernissage 0. 29 django.db.models rows generate 846 edges\n      in a Django application.\n\nTHE COST THIS ITEM DID NOT ANTICIPATE, and the reason the cohort number is not\nquotable. Verdicts moved 0 of 20 -- but the cohort holds 12 violated and 8\ninconclusive and NO `confirmed` verdict, and confirmed is the only value that\ncan degrade. Checking the cohort contained the culled ROWS was necessary and not\nsufficient; the population this claim is about is confirmed verdicts.\n\nPOSITIVE CONTROL: a repo whose only external call lands in a relocated module\ngoes confirmed rc 0 -> inconclusive rc 2, the tool naming django.db.models as\n\"never examined\". That is #598's \"an unvouched row does not EXAMINE\" composing\nwith ruling 1. THIS ITEM'S RISK STATEMENT COVERS ONLY THE --no-default-overlays\nPATH; this fires on a DEFAULT run. It is the ruled behaviour and it fails\nCLOSED, but it is a user-visible exit-code change for any repository whose I/O\nis reached through Django / Phoenix / SwiftNIO / Wai.\n\nREMEDY, CHECKED not merely offered: passing the same overlay via --io-primitives\nre-vouches the rows and restores confirmed rc 0 with user_supplied: true --\nthe user may vouch for their own dependencies; hypergumbo may not on their\nbehalf.\n\nRULING 6 VERIFIED LIVE: per-language stderr naming each file and its retrieved:\nfloor, silent under --no-default-overlays. Floors are 2026-03-20..2026-04-15 and\ndeliberately were NOT moved to today -- these rows were relocated, not\nre-checked upstream.\n\nFull suite on the final tree: 24,585 passed / 0 failed, mypy ratchet clean."  # 5fc1
