- op: discuss  # 4008
  at: '2026-08-28T21:08:32Z'  # 4008
  by: agent  # 4008
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4008
  clock: 5  # 4008
  nonce: '4008'  # 4008
  message: "DONE, verified ON MERGED dev (PR #613 = c3e64fe7cc; count correction #614 = 7e85567aba).\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE, not the branch:\n  scope gate      15 catalogues, out-of-scope = NONE\n  rows served from overlays: elixir 144, python 92, go 53, haskell 43, swift 38\n  HIGH_RISK phantom check   PASS (execabs resolves FROM THE OVERLAY)\n  erlang http_client        gone\n  check-self-claims         18/18 unchanged, exit 0, snapshot NOT re-recorded\n  full suite                24,585 passed / 0 failed, mypy ratchet clean\n\nTHE COUNT I PUBLISHED WAS WRONG AND IS FIXED (#614). I said 293 relocated rows\nin the commit, PR and changelog; the real figure is 291, and the changelog entry\ncontradicted its own breakdown (144+43+38+33+33). 293 summed the gate's\nPER-LANGUAGE stray counts, which double-count `http_client` (elixir inherits it\nfrom the erlang parent) and include a row that was DELETED rather than moved.\nExact: 291 relocated + 1 deleted = 292 distinct out-of-scope rows. The spec was\nwrong a second way -- it credited all of them to \"the eight ungated languages\",\nbut python HAD a gate: the eight ungated held 259, and python held the other 33\ninside a DENYLIST gate that could not see them, which is a sharper argument for\nthe shape change than the wrong number was.\n\nWHAT CI CAUGHT THAT I DID NOT, and it is the best part of this item.\n`check-self-claims` failed with ALL EIGHTEEN of hypergumbo's own claims dropping\nconfirmed_with_caveats -> inconclusive. Chain: hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py calls\n`uvicorn.run`; uvicorn was one of the four relocated python residue rows;\nrelocated => unvouched; an unvouched row does not EXAMINE (#598); uvicorn enters\nthe uncatalogued-module list; and `_boundary_coverage` grants an opaque launch a\nQUALIFIED verdict only when that list is empty (`qualifying_only=not unknown`).\nONE ENTRY WITHHELD EIGHTEEN VERDICTS. The empty caveat lists and credited_flows\nnonzero->zero the gate also reported are DOWNSTREAM of that single flip, not\nfour regressions -- the details string still reported 14 sanitized flows while\n`sanitized_flows` read 0. Control: the same gate on dev said \"18 claims\nunchanged\", so the drift was mine.\n\nTHE FIX WAS TO OBEY THE RULING, NOT TO RE-RECORD. `--update` was available and\nwould have turned CI green in one command; that gate exists because a self-proof\nonce \"improved\" to all-confirmed while its credited flows collapsed 2,658 -> 0.\nThe downgrade would also have been FALSE -- hypergumbo's behaviour did not\nchange, only its willingness to vouch for one row. uvicorn is now declared in\ndocs/io-primitives-overlays/hypergumbo-self.yaml beside starlette, where every\nother hypergumbo dependency already lives; it was missing only because the\nshipped catalogue had been carrying it, which IS the drift ADR-0047 corrects.\nSnapshot restored exactly, 18/18, no update. hypergumbo dogfooded the\nconsequence of its own ruling and applied the remedy any user would.\n\nCLOSES-BY-EXECUTION: WI-sutuk and WI-bahid are both `done` with their own\nevidence notes."  # 4008
